\ A tactic proof closed by by-sorry, Lean's sorry tactic (plan FE1g-3;
\ ADR 0021 Amendment 1). Lean: theorem zero_add_sorry (n : Nat) : 0 + n = n
\ := by sorry is accepted with the warning "declaration uses `sorry`" and
\ depends on sorryAx (tests/front/tactic-run.lean). Today 0 and + wait for
\ plans FE1e5 and S2: the text stops at end with error 139, exit 2.
\ tests/front/tactic-run.fs runs it with stand-in elaborators: with this
\ statement, by-sorry needs the level of 0 + n = n, which type inference
\ cannot find while a text runs, before the library is fed (error 93,
\ until plan FE1e lets the Meta layer see the library); with the stand-in
\ statement p for a variable p : Prop instead (natural LeanForth cannot
\ write Prop yet, plan FE2), the kernel accepts it, NOT PROVED, and the
\ open part is reported.
theorem zero_add_sorry
  Nat explicit: n
  0 n + n =
:= by
  by-sorry
end zero_add_sorry
